One valid approach starts with:

$brand: #3157d5;
.button { padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; }
.button--primary { background: $brand; color: white; }
.button--secondary { background: transparent; border: 1px solid $brand; }
.button--disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: not-allowed; }

Then compile it with Dart Sass and review the generated CSS. Acceptance depends on the exact prompt and evidence, not on matching the starter byte-for-byte.
